,title,link,text,language,family
0,Nuxalk - Wikipedia,https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuxalk,"I Nuxalk, anche noti come Bella Coola o Bellacoola, sono un popolo indigeno, delle cosiddette First Nations del Canada, che vivevano nell'area della città di Bella Coola in Columbia Britannica. Il loro governo tribale è denominato Nuxalk Nation.",Bella Coola,Salish
1,Bella Coola Language (BLC) – L1 & L2 Speakers... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/blc/,Bella Coola is an endangered indigenous language of Canada. It belongs to the Salish language family. The language is used as a first language by the elderly only.,Bella Coola,Salish
2,Why We Should Stop Calling it the Salish Sea | Post Alley,https://www.postalley.org/2021/04/20/why-we-should-stop-calling-it-the-salish-sea/,"Linguists continued the work, and the term (rendered now as Salish or Salishan) identifies 23 separate languages grouped into three families: Interior Salish, spoken in British Columbia, and much of the Pacific Northwest; Bella Coola Salish, spoken on Bella Coola Inlet in British Columbia...",Bella Coola,Salish
3,"Salish Language and the Spokane, Kalispel, and Flathead Salish...",https://www.native-languages.org/salish.htm,"Salish language samples and resources. Flathead Salish Culture and History.Salish Placenames: Pacific Northwest place names in Spokane, Lushootseed, Shuswap, Straits Salish, Bella Coola, and Coeur d'Alene.",Bella Coola,Salish
4,Bella Coola | Accent Network,https://accentnetwork.com/bella-coola/,"Salish. Bella Coola, Canada.Bella Coola language, Canada. Salishan language family. Spoken in British Columbia by approximately 20 people. Market Insights. Oral traditions and storytelling are important in Bella Coola culture.",Bella Coola,Salish
5,Salish Myths and Legends: One People's Stories (Native Literatures of...,https://epdf.pub/salish-myths-and-legends-one-peoples-stories-native-literatures-of-the-americas.html,"Bella Coola also shows interesting cognate words with Interior Salish, including that for “¿sher” (Martes pennanti) with distant Coeur d’Alene. Kinkade (1990:205) presents a cogent argument for an Interior origin for Bella Coola. Origins and Migrations | xvii.",Bella Coola,Salish
6,Famille salishenne,https://www.axl.cefan.ulaval.ca/amnord/cnddemofamindien_salishenne.htm,"bella-coola. Salish du Centre.Les langues de la famille salishenne comptent plusieurs variétés tant sur la côte du Pacifique que de l'intérieur. Ainsi, le bella-coola compte trois dialectes, le halkomelem trois ou quatre, l'okanagan plusieurs, le shuswap deux, le salish plusieurs dialectes.",Bella Coola,Salish
7,Anahim%2BLake - Bella Coola - British Columbia Travel and...,https://britishcolumbia.com/plan-your-trip/regions-and-towns/cariboo-chilcotin-coast/bella-coola/locality/Anahim%2BLake/,"Long the home of the Coast Salish Nuxalk people, the Bella Coola Valley became a route to the Cariboo gold fields in 1858, the location of a Hudson’s Bay Company trading post in 1867, and a home for Norwegian colonists from Minnesota.",Bella Coola,Salish
8,1886: Victoria-style Chinuk Wawa song from Nuxalks... | Chinook Jargon,https://chinookjargon.com/2021/11/01/1886-victoria-style-chinuk-wawa-song-from-nuxalks-in-germany-and-a-grammatical-mystery/,"A group of 9 Nuxalk people (""Bella Coola"" Salish) from the British Columbia coast visited Germany in 1885-1886, performing various songs and dances that they knew. They had been brought by Captain Adrian Jacobsen and his brother Philipp, who we have read about previously on my site. …",Bella Coola,Salish
9,ICSNL 48 Cover,https://lingpapers.sites.olt.ubc.ca/files/2018/01/2013_Nater.pdf,"How Salish is Bella Coola? Hank Nater.4 Bella Coola vocabulary with unknown origin. Below, I list those BC verbo-nominal stems and roots that I have not. been able to relate to other Salish and/or NS.",Bella Coola,Salish
